NODE id=matrix/router/internal/finance.Service.serve kind=method
  digest=b3:769191e1a42292bf73004f28c623e4d82e5065db6a67ef85f2204e13ef77871e file=router/internal/finance/service.go range=113:164 lang=go exported=false byte_range=3355:5212
  sig=func (s *Service) serve(ctx context.Context, r req, primary func(context.Context) (any, error), fallback func(context.Context) (any, error)) (any, Source, error)
  doc=serve is the one path every finance call takes: rate limit, cache with\nsingle-flight collapse, primary provider, declared fallback on a retryable\nfailure, then the metering record.\n\nThe fallback is only tried when the primary's failure is retryable — a\nmalformed request or a genuine "no such symbol" is not worth a second vendor\ncall, and burning the fallback's quota on it would be the expensive kind of\nwrong.
